Z||000000||2M4 Dale||12-28-2000||10:15 AM||||Anyone have a parts code book ???<P>The fellow I got this engine from says it was destined for 1989 Fiero production.<P>This engine I just aquired has the following identification marks on it.<P>On the machined pad on the block behind the water pump are the following stamped numbers.<P>A080821CFC<P>On the block in front of the right clyinder head (looking at it from the water pump end) cast into the block are the following numbers.<P>10065459<P>On the block below the right clyinder head.<P>GM  2.8L  G<P>On the right side of the pan is a sticker with these numbers.<P>        CFC<BR> *10CFCA708211481*<P>Don't really matter...it would just be neat to know...Ya know...lol||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||12-28-2000||10:59 AM||||Dale,<P>I would say that Dave Kruzalach (I know his last name is spelled differently... damn engineers spelling ability!) would be your best bet.  He is the guy that has every piece of Fiero literature out there.  He should at least know what doccumentation is needed to decode these numbers.  I have the Helms and MVMA manuals but do not think that I have the information to get what you want.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
